# English-only artifacts

**Prompt language does not change output language.** Chat may be Dutch or English; the artifacts below are always **English**.

## Must be English

- Specs and plans (`.agents/specs/**`, `.agents/plans/**`, `docs/plans/**`)
- Documentation (`docs/**`, package docs, READMEs, skills)
- GitHub issue titles and bodies (Goals, Epics, Tasks, Chores, Bugs)
- GitHub issue comments, including automated comments
- PR titles, descriptions, review comments, and replies
- Anything posted via `gh` or the GitHub API
- Commit messages

Write English on the first create — do not file Dutch and translate later.

## Out of scope

- **User chat** may stay Dutch or English as the user writes
- **Code comments** may follow the existing language of the file
- **Product / fixture strings** (`nl-NL` samples, locale files) may be Dutch
- Do **not** rewrite historical GitHub **comments** unless asked
- **Do** translate Dutch issue/PR **bodies** and **repo docs** when found

Canonical policy: [`.agents/skills/developer/english-only.md`](../../.agents/skills/developer/english-only.md). CI: `pnpm run check:agent-docs`.

## Examples

```text
❌ BAD (Dutch on GitHub / in a spec)
De tiebreaker is deterministic op lex-min.

✅ GOOD
The tiebreaker is deterministic on lex-min.
```
